# Eth1DataCache — Requested Elements

## Field Declarations

The class holds a `Spec` reference alongside voting period configuration and metric gauges:

```java
private final Spec spec;
private final Eth1VotingPeriod eth1VotingPeriod;
private final UInt64 cacheDuration;

private final NavigableMap<UInt64, Eth1DataAndHeight> eth1ChainCache = new ConcurrentSkipListMap<>();
private final SettableGauge currentPeriodVotesTotal;
private final SettableGauge currentPeriodVotesUnknown;
private final SettableGauge currentPeriodVotesCurrent;
private final SettableGauge currentPeriodVotesBest;
private final SettableGauge currentPeriodVotesMax;
```

## Constructor Signature

```java
public Eth1DataCache(
    final Spec spec, final MetricsSystem metricsSystem, final Eth1VotingPeriod eth1VotingPeriod)
```

The constructor assigns the three parameters to fields, derives `cacheDuration` from the voting period, and registers the cache-size gauge plus five vote-tracking gauges.

## getEth1Vote

The `Spec` is used first to short-circuit when the older deposit mechanism is off:

```java
if (spec.isFormerDepositMechanismDisabled(state)) {
  // no need for a real vote when Eth1 polling has been disabled
  return state.getEth1Data();
}
```

When still active, the method builds a set of valid blocks, counts votes, determines a default vote (last considered entry, or the state's own data if none), then picks the highest-value vote restricted to valid blocks, falling back to the default vote otherwise.

## updateMetrics

The same `Spec` check gates metric updates and returns early when disabled:

```java
if (spec.isFormerDepositMechanismDisabled(state)) {
  // no need to update metrics when Eth1 polling has been disabled
  return;
}
```

Otherwise it computes the set of known blocks, tallies votes, and sets each gauge: max possible votes, total votes cast, unknown-block votes, current-data votes, and the leading (best) vote count.

## How Spec Is Used

In both methods, `Spec` serves a single purpose: calling `isFormerDepositMechanismDisabled(state)` to decide whether Eth1 polling logic should run at all. When that returns true, `getEth1Vote` returns the state's existing Eth1 data directly and `updateMetrics` skips all gauge updates.

